## Security significance

The test confirms XXE injection. The weakness occurs when an application processes untrusted XML while allowing the parser to resolve external entities.

Successful exploitation can expose files readable by the application process. Depending on parser capabilities and network permissions, XXE may also enable server-side requests to internal or external services. These additional impacts should only be reported as demonstrated findings when separately tested.


## Recommendations

- Disable Document Type Definitions and external entity resolution in the XML parser.
- Disable external DTD loading, external schema retrieval, and XInclude processing where supported and unnecessary.
- Use a maintained XML parser with explicitly configured security settings.
- Validate XML against a trusted local schema when appropriate. Schema validation must supplement secure parser settings.
- Run the application with minimal filesystem permissions and restrict unnecessary outbound network access.
- Return generic client-facing errors while keeping detailed diagnostics in protected server logs.
- Add regression tests confirming that external entity references cannot disclose files or trigger unauthorized network requests.

